Currently, dict comprehension is not supported by JIT but it is widely used in python codes. Is there any plans to support it?
class MyModule(nn.Module):
    def forward(self):
        x = {i: i for i in range(2)}
        return x

model = MyModule()
model_s = torch.jit.script(model)

we will get:
torch.jit.frontend.UnsupportedNodeError: DictComp aren't supported:
  File "main_test.py", line 6
    def forward(self):
        x = {i: i for i in range(2)}
            ~ <--- HERE
        return x

we may use a for-loop to gradually add elements to the dict as a workaround, but it's a pretty bad user experience.
